# Line-ending policy.
#
# The MindFlock engine runs on Linux / inside WSL, so shell scripts MUST be
# checked out with LF on every platform. Without this, git on Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites *.sh to CRLF on checkout, and the Windows
# Electron build then packages an install.sh that dash/bash inside WSL refuses
# to run — failing on the very first command with:
#
#     install.sh: 38: set: Illegal option -
#
*.sh            text eol=lf
install.sh      text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf

# Windows-only helper scripts stay CRLF.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Binary assets — never touch line endings or try to diff them as text.
*.png           binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.icns          binary
*.mp4           binary
*.whl           binary
